<%#
  REISSUE REFUSED — the current PIN has already been used

  Route:  POST /admin/participants/:participantNumber/reissue-pin  (409)
  Layout: nav: 'admin'

  Locals
    title        String
    participant  Object
    usage        Object  { used, pinIssuedAt, lastSignedInAt }

  A PIN may be regenerated freely while untried — that is when distribution
  mistakes surface. Once the officer has signed in it has done its job, and
  changing it disrupts them.

  Refused, not forbidden. An officer who signs in one day and loses their slip
  before the next would otherwise have no route back in. The override below is a
  separate deliberate action and is audited distinctly.
%>

<div class="container container-narrow section">

  <div class="label-meta">Reissue refused</div>
  <h1 style="font-size:clamp(24px,3vw,32px)">
    <%= participant.full_name %> has already used this PIN
  </h1>

  <div class="alert alert-danger" role="alert" style="margin-bottom:var(--sp-5)">
    This officer signed in with their current PIN, so it is no longer an unused
    slip that can be quietly replaced. Issuing a new one will lock them out of
    the PIN they are holding.
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <table class="data-table" style="min-width:0">
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td style="width:44%;color:var(--text-muted)">Officer</td>
          <td><strong><%= participant.full_name %></strong>
              &middot; <span class="font-mono">#<%= participant.participant_number %></span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td style="color:var(--text-muted)">Current PIN issued</td>
          <td class="font-mono"><%= usage.pinIssuedAt %></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border-bottom:0">
          <td style="color:var(--text-muted)">Officer signed in</td>
          <td class="font-mono"><%= usage.lastSignedInAt %></td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h3 style="margin-top:var(--sp-6)">If they have genuinely lost access</h3>
  <p class="text-muted" style="max-width:64ch">
    Issue a replacement anyway. Their current PIN stops working immediately, so
    only do this if you can hand them the new one. It is recorded in the audit
    log as an override, distinct from a routine reissue.
  </p>

  <div class="row" style="gap:var(--sp-3);margin-top:var(--sp-4)">
    <form method="POST"
          action="/admin/participants/<%= participant.participant_number %>/reissue-pin"
          onsubmit="return confirm('Issue a replacement PIN for <%= participant.full_name.replace(/'/g, "\\'") %> anyway?\n\nThey have already signed in with their current PIN. It will stop working the moment you confirm, so make sure you can hand them the new one.');">
      <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= typeof csrfToken !== 'undefined' ? csrfToken : '' %>">
      <input type="hidden" name="override" value="1">
      <button type="submit" class="btn btn-terracotta">Issue replacement anyway</button>
    </form>
    <a href="/admin/participants" class="btn btn-ghost">Back to roster</a>
  </div>

</div>
